    "intro": "Most pressure washing estimates are lost to silence, not to a lower price. The homeowner asked three companies, one answered the same day with a clear quote, and the other two sent something vague a week later or never followed up. Winning more of your quotes is less about cutting your price and more about what goes on the estimate, how quickly it arrives, and what happens when the customer goes quiet. This post covers the estimate itself: what to include, how to word it, when to send it, and how to follow up without being a pest.",
