        "content": "On a lawn route, a full day is a good day. On a wash schedule, a completely full week is a problem waiting to happen. You will lose days to wind and rain, and those jobs have to go somewhere.\n\nA simple approach is to leave part of each week unbooked during peak season, or to keep one day a week as a flex day that absorbs rain-outs. If nothing gets rained out, use the flex day for smaller jobs from the Waiting List: a sidewalk here, a set of trash cans there, the jobs that fit anywhere.\n\nKeep a short list of customers who said \"any time is fine.\" These are the jobs you slide into a gap when a big job cancels. Note on the property that the customer is flexible and that the crew does not need them home, provided the spigot is outside and the gate is left open. Those notes are what make last-minute rearranging possible."
