        "h2": "Sharing Crews With Lawn Routes",
        "content": "If your wash work borrows people or trucks from mowing, decide the rules early. A common setup is that mowing has priority on route days, and washing takes the slow days, the days after heavy rain when turf is too wet to cut cleanly, and the gaps in early spring and late fall. Another is a dedicated wash truck with one or two people who can jump onto a mowing crew when wash work is thin.\n\nEither way, keep both kinds of work on the same calendar. When the wash jobs live in a separate notebook, you double-book people and nobody notices until the morning of. With every truck's day on one schedule, you can see whether Thursday's wash job collides with Thursday's mowing route before it happens.\n\nRecurring lawn services and one-time wash jobs behave differently, and that is fine. The mowing repeats every 7 days on its own. Wash jobs come off the Waiting List when you schedule them. The [scheduling features page](/features/field-service-scheduling-software) shows how both show up together on the calendar and the Scheduled list."
