        "content": "Small jobs still carry the drive, the setup and the cleanup. A 150 square foot patio at 18 cents is $27, which does not cover the trip. Set a minimum ticket that covers at least the first hour or so of a crew's time, including the drive.\n\nMany companies set one minimum for customers inside their main service area and a higher one outside it. Others set a minimum and then encourage small jobs to add something: \"Our minimum is $150; for that we can do your patio and front walk.\"\n\nA minimum also protects you from \"can you just do this one spot\" calls that eat a whole morning. Tell people the minimum up front, put it on the estimate, and stick to it unless you are already on their street for another job that day."
