        "h2": "Price Add-Ons and Extras Separately",
        "content": "The base job is only part of the ticket. Add-ons often make the difference between a decent job and a good one, and they are easy to sell when they are listed with a price.\n\nCommon add-ons include oil and rust stain treatment (priced separately and with no guarantee), gutter face brightening, fences, trash cans, mailbox and lamppost, window rinsing, and sealing after a paver or concrete clean. Each has its own time and material cost; price it on its own line.\n\nDo not give add-ons away to win the job. If you throw in the trash cans for free once, the customer expects it next year. Instead, offer a modest bundle price: house wash plus driveway for a little less than the two separately. The customer sees a deal, and you get two services on one trip, which is where the real savings are.\n\nUpsell alerts after a job can bring add-ons back later: a fall message to driveway customers about sealing, or a spring note to house wash customers about the fence."
