    "intro": "A pressure washing job depends on the customer more than a mowing visit does. Someone has to turn on the spigot, move the cars, close the windows, put the dog inside and open the gate. When they forget, your crew loses an hour or the job does not happen. Texting is the most reliable way to get those things done, because people read texts. This post covers which messages to send, what to say in each, how to handle replies, and how to keep your messages short enough that they do not cost more than they should.",
