        "h2": "On the Way and Arrived",
        "content": "Many wash customers want to be home when you start, or at least know when you are coming so they can leave the gate open. A \"you're next\" or on-the-way text gives them a heads-up: \"Our crew is heading to your house now, about 15 minutes out.\"\n\nThat text also saves the crew time. A customer who knows you are coming moves the car before you arrive instead of while you wait.\n\nA tech-arrived text is useful for customers who are not home. It tells them the crew is on site and working, which matters for homeowners who are nervous about strangers in the backyard. If the customer has a question (\"Can you also do the back steps?\"), they can answer while the crew is still there.\n\nIf the owner turns on the live route map for customers on their service day, they can watch the truck approach, which cuts down on \"when will you be here\" calls."
