        "h2": "Two-Way Texting and Keeping Messages Short",
        "content": "Customers reply to texts. \"Can you also do the patio?\" \"The spigot is behind the AC unit.\" \"I need to move it to Friday.\" Two-way texting lets those replies land in the office where someone can answer, instead of on a tech's personal phone. In IndustryBossPro, two-way texting is on the Pro plan ($89 a month) and the Crew plan.\n\nTexts are counted in segments, and both sent and received messages count. A standard segment is about 160 plain characters. Longer messages split into several segments, and certain characters, like curly quotes, emoji and some dashes, switch the message to a format that holds far fewer characters per segment. A night-before text that runs to 300 characters with an emoji in it can cost three or four segments instead of two.\n\nSo keep messages tight. Use plain punctuation. Cut the greetings and sign-offs down. Put the important instruction first. A message that fits in one or two segments gets read faster and costs less. The [mobile app features page](/features/field-service-mobile-app) shows how the crew side of these alerts works."
